\section{Compare the Plans as Well as the Results}

Run \verb|gcc -### main.o bias.o -o check| to print the planned commands without executing them, and compare that with a trace of \verb|gcc -### main.c bias.c -o check|. The latter also includes the work needed to produce each object. The exact startup objects, paths, and choice of link helper vary with installation and options. Replacing the driver with a bare \texttt{ld} call without recreating its inputs does not normally reproduce a hosted C link: the presence of a C function named \texttt{main} is not by itself a machine entry point.

The useful regression invariant is behavioral: with the same source, headers, target, and relevant options, splitting the build at stable artifact boundaries should preserve the observable result. Temporary filenames, debug metadata, and other incidental bytes need not agree. When moving output between toolchains, check the target ABI as well as the file format. Two objects can both be ELF and still target different machines or incompatible calling conventions.
